<code>assert list != null => this.size() == list.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < list.size(); this.get(i).equals(list.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(list == null) => this.equals(new RoleList(\old(list)));</code>

However, since the `RoleList` constructor is being called within the same context and we need to compare the constructed object with the input list, we should directly compare `this` with the input list using the `containsAll` and `size` methods:

<code>assert !\old(list == null) => this.containsAll(\old(list)) && this.size() == \old(list).size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(list == null) => this.equals(new RoleList(\old(list)));</code>
